==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-eat up.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|<,,ate,eaten>}}

# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[consume]] completely.
#: {{cot|en|drink up}}
#: {{ux|en|He was so hungry that he '''ate up''' everything on his plate.}}
#: {{ux|en|Dinner is served. '''Eat up'''!}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang|figurative}} To cause (someone) to obsess; to figuratively consume (someone).
#: {{ux|en|His anger has been '''eating''' him '''up'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figurative}} To [[subtract]], [[use up]].
#: {{ux|en|His behavior has '''eaten up''' all the goodwill we felt towards him.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1934|author=Frank Richards|title=The Magnet: The Mystery of the Vaults
|passage=The powerful car '''ate up''' the miles.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figurative|informal}} To [[accept]] or [[believe]] entirely, [[immediately]], and without [[question]]ing.
#: {{ux|en|She '''ate up''' everything that her image consultant said.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To [[acclaim]] or [[praise]] (someone or something); to [[consume]] {{gloss|[[absorb]] [[information]]}}.
#: {{ux|en|They '''eat up''' every book he puts out.}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|date=1977-11-13|author=Robert Sherman|title=Beguiling ‘Devil's Disciple’|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/nMiqk|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1977/11/13/archives/westchester-weekly-beguiling-devils-disciple-music.html|archivedate=3 December 2025|passage=There are a number of subsidiary plots and characters that don't ring entirely true, and the ending is straight out of “The Perils of Pauline,” but I '''ate''' it all '''up''' anyway, because in the last analysis the opera has a kind of honest, disarming sentimentality.}}
#* {{RQ:LATimes|date=1992-01-09|author=John Balzar|quotee=Michael Poboronchook|title=Russians Lose Their Country on Way to New World{{nb...|: Three ships set out to trace Bering’s route to Alaska. But they are stranded by the breakup of the Soviet Union.}}|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251203142531/https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-1992-01-09-mn-2138-story.html|passage=When I was 13 years old and very ill in a hospital, my father gave me a book about a man who went around the world, a Czech . . . . I did not read that book, I ''ate'', I '''ate''' it '''up'''. I decided then, I too will go around the world, whether by bicycle or boat or on my belly like a snake.}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|date=2020-06-09|author=Margaret Lyons|quotee=Priya|title=What Should I Watch After I’ve Binged ‘Dead to Me’?|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200609141017/https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/09/arts/television/dead-to-me-santa-clarita-diet.html|passage=Without thinking much about “Dead To Me,” I '''ate''' it all '''up''' quickly during this quarantine time. I love it so much. It’s short, zippy, interesting and twisty without ever being complicated. Is there anything else in this vein that you can recommend?}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|date=2024-07-11|author=Theodore Schleifer|title=How Biden Lost George Clooney and Hollywood|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240711233126/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/11/us/politics/biden-george-clooney-hollywood.html|author2=Jacob Bernstein|author3=Reid J. Epstein|passage=Onstage at the fund-raiser beside Mr. Obama and Jimmy Kimmel, Mr. Biden laughed along, cracked a joke or two, and slammed the Supreme Court. The audience '''ate''' it '''up'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|US|informal|chiefly|of children or pets}} To find something to be very [[cute]].
#: {{ux|en|You're so cute, I could just '''eat you up'''!}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang|figurative}} To go quickly on a route.
#: {{ux|en|We '''ate up''' the road to Pennsylvania.}}
#: {{ux|en|You're gonna have to '''eat up''' the whole way there.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To be very [[good]] at; to [[succeed]] at; to [[smash]]. {{n-g|(Compare {{m|en|eat and leave no crumbs}}.)}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023-07-14|author=Anwaya Mane|title=“THEY ATE THAT UP”: BTS’ Jungkook’s fans lavish praise on Bangtan’s maknae and Han So-hee’s crackling chemistry in SEVEN MV|journal=w:Sportskeeda|url=https://www.sportskeeda.com/pop-culture/they-ate-that-up-bts-jungkook-s-fans-lavish-praise-bangtan-s-maknae-han-so-hee-s-crackling-chemistry-seven-mv|passage=One fan shared a snippet from the music video wherein Jungkook and Han So-hee are drowning in water. Despite the catastrophic situation, the lovers are squabbling with each other. The fan commented: “{{smallcaps|The laundromat cause they '''ate''' that '''up'''}}”.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230719092301/https://www.sportskeeda.com/pop-culture/they-ate-that-up-bts-jungkook-s-fans-lavish-praise-bangtan-s-maknae-han-so-hee-s-crackling-chemistry-seven-mv|archivedate=19 July 2023}}
# {{lb|en|slang|informal}} To completely dominate someone else, especially with a [[comeback]] or [[clapback]].
#: {{ux|en|Girl, you '''ate''' him '''up'''!}}

